build.host_notes:
host_mode 1500, seed 6350. `mr_lib.py preview Closure-110 com/google/javascript/rhino/Node.java 5` draws DefaultPassConfig (2458 lines), parsing/parser/Parser (2378), rhino/jstype/JSTypeRegistry (1830), regex/RegExpTree (1859) and parsing/JsDocInfoParser (2571). Further draws: NodeUtil, CompilerOptions, jsonml/Reader, SymbolTable, JSDocInfo, Compiler, TypeCheck.

This is a recipe-level problem for every Closure instance, not only this one. Closure indents with 2 spaces, but host_search.pick_insertion_anchor keeps only methods indented exactly 4 spaces. In Closure those are all methods of nested classes. So every seeded anchor that is found lands inside a nested type:
- the hop-1 anchor (seed 6450) lands in DefaultPassConfig.GlobalTypeResolver, a non-static inner class, where a static method does not compile;
- RegExpTree lands in Anchor, Concatenation and similar package-private nested classes;
- JsDocInfoParser lands in the private ExtractionInfo;
- NodeUtil lands in package-private or private predicates;
- Reader lands in a private ErrorReporter;
- CompilerOptions lands in a nested enum;
- SymbolTable, JSDocInfo and Compiler land in public static nested classes (Symbol, SymbolScope, Marker, CodeBuilder).

Only Parser, JSTypeRegistry and TypeCheck have no indent-4 methods, so the hop goes in their outer class (end of class). Under the reading "a hop must be a member of the drawn host class", only 3 of the 12 hosts in the 1500 pool are usable. Under a looser reading (a static method that compiles and can be reached from the caller's package), five hosts could be found, but some hops would then sit in public static nested classes such as SymbolTable.Symbol. Not built, so nothing was substituted.

